WEBVTT

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.650
<i>Ten AM...</i>

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>Eagle Jump employees begin their workday.</i>

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:16.570
<i></i>Moon Ranger<i> Final Live general 
admission tickets go on sale...</i>

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.240
<i>...now!</i>

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.000
<i>I'm going to get them, no matter what!</i>

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.840
<b>Magical Girl
Moon Ranger</b>

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.840
<i></i>Moon Ranger<i>...</i>

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.850
<b>Magical Girl Moon Ranger R</b>

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.490
<i>Originally an anime for young girls,</i>

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.850
<i>its high quality earned it 
an adult following, as well.</i>

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:08.480
<i>The insert songs are highly regarded and 
the concerts have been huge hits.</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.730
All seats: 4500 yen

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.730
16:00 Show (15:30 Doors)

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.730
<i>I had no luck with 
the pre-order ticket lottery.</i>

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:16.500
<i>So right now... If I don't get them here, 
I won't have another chance!</i>

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.950
The server is under heavy load
 This site is currently receiving heavy traffic and 
may be hard to connect to. We apologize for any 
inconvenience this may cause our users. Please 
try accessing the site again after a few minutes.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.450
<i>The ticket site is down!</i>

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:30.490
<i>It was so much easier back when 
they held them at smaller venues.</i>

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.710
<i>But that was a year and a half ago.</i>

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.490
<i>After two and a half years, 
</i>Moon Ranger<i> finally ends this March.</i>

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.610
<i>But the new series starts April, 
with a new heroine.</i>

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.260
<i>I'm torn between sadness and anticipation.</i>

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.100
<i>But this is our last chance to show 
the first gen legends our support!</i>

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.730
<i>So please, just connect! 
For the love of God, connect!</i>

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.250
<b>30 minutes later</b>

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.490
They're sold out?!

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.200
Slacking on the job?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.160
Y-You've gotta understand...

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.650
I understand you were slacking.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.290
Are you crazy? Everyone else is hard at work.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.720
I know. I was going to make up 
for it by working during lunch.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.410
Well, that's good.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:21.520
Someone like Yagami-san wouldn't 
have let you off as easy as I did.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.800
Yeah...

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.700
You need to be more careful.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.100
Sorry...

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.980
Mozuku, it's lunchtime.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.960
Go ahead. Eat your fill.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.990
Hajime-chan...

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.940
What is it, Hifumi-senpai?

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:01.920
I overheard you and Yun-chan... 
in the bathroom...

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.370
I'm so sorry! But I really 
wanted those tickets!

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:10.040
N-No... that's not what I meant...

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.990
To tell you the truth... 
I was doing the same thing...

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:20.820
It's just one seat... but I was able 
to get one... for the evening show.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.570
<b>So jelly</b>

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.210
<i>So jelly, so jelly, so jelly...</i>

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:28.510
S-So... seeing as you like <i>
Moon Ranger</i> more than I do...

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:33.960
Would you... like my ticket...?

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.290
<b>Want</b>

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.290
<i>Want, want, want!</i>

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.850
N-No, I couldn't!

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:42.550
You nabbed that ticket, 
so you should be the one to go!

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.470
Of course, I really want to go,

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.060
but you got that ticket because 
you like <i>Moon Ranger</i>, too.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.560
You want to support 
<i>Moon Ranger</i> just as much as I!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.230
So please, show them enough 
fan spirit for the both of us!

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.400
Okay...

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.400
That's good enough for me... Thank you.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.080
Mixed Sandwiches

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.080
Here.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:15.660
You won't make it through 
the day on an empty stomach.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.900
Thanks.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:20.790
Honestly, you're such a handful. 
You're just like a kid.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:26.010
Also... I have an adult chaperon ticket 
for the afternoon show.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:26.910
Huh?

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.360
My little brother and sister, Ren and Miu,

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.270
also love <i>Moon Ranger</i>, so we got tickets.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.690
The three of us were 
planning to go with my dad,

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.330
but he's not really interested 
in stuff like that to begin with.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.780
So I asked, and he said you could have his.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:47.570
You can't wave around those 
glowy stick things at this show,

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.410
but are you still interested?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.530
I love you, Yun!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.270
Hey— Y-You're smothering me!

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.270
Yun-sama!

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.830
Yun! Yun! Yun!

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.990
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.180
Hajime-oneechan!

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.880
I missed you!

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:16.690
Same here! Congrats on 
getting into elementary school!

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:17.890
Me, too! Me, too!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.900
Mega Particle... Requiem...

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.900
Shoot!

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:27.410
<i>And now there are three kids.</i>

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.460
Adults aren't allowed to stand.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.870
Yeah, I know.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.750
It's starting!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.550
Sit down!

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:49.550
Thanks for coming today, everyone!

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.050
Mega Particle... Requiem...

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.970
Shoot!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:03.310
Thanks, everyone! All right, let's get 
things started with our first song!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.570
<i>Danger's nothing to a magical pretty girl</i>

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.320
<i>It's so unbelievably wonderful</i>

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.260
<i>I'm going cast a spell so serious</i>

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.080
<i>That it'll steal your heart</i>

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:27.130
<i>Though we may hold back 
tears in the face of evil...</i>

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:31.090
Thank you so much, everyone! See you again!

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.390
Bye-bye!

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.030
About a year ago, they were so 
nervous when they sang live...

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.630
Just look at how far they've come.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:46.900
And to think, now I get to witness them 
passing the torch to the next generation!

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.900
I'm so touched!

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.910
Seeing you this happy 
makes me glad I invited you.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:56.700
Thanks! I really do love you, Yun!

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.540
A-As long as you're grateful.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.650
All right. Let's do this!

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.360
Huh? Hifumi-senpai?

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.760
Aoba-chan? Nene-chan?

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.350
What a coincidence!

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.730
So you also emerged victorious 
from that ruthless battle?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.730
Actually, sorry to disturb 
you on your day off.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.230
We even ended up in adjacent seats.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.590
I-It's no big deal...

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:34.210
All the better! Let's enjoy this together.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:35.640
Yeah!

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.780
Y-Yeah!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.540
Man, it was so much fun!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.340
The concert was so amazing!

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:49.480
I had a lot of fun, too. 
I owe it to Nenecchi for inviting me.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.300
And I owe it all to Yun.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.530
Right?

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.050
Yeah, I get it already.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.260
Did Hifumi-senpai get really 
into the concert, too?

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.930
Well...

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.410
Mega Particle... Requiem...

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.980
Shoot!

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:11.350
Yes! She seemed to be having a lot of fun.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:23.930
Beary, beary, beary, 
how beary scary you are...

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.830
Beary-bear... Beary-bear.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:42.760
<i>Well, knowing Hifumin, I probably just 
startled her off by making eye contact.</i>

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:44.660
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.770
<i>I must have... looked suspicious to her.</i>

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.910
<i>Talk about awkward silence.</i>

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.160
<i>But, seriously...</i>

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.570
<i>Why was she smiling?</i>

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.680
<i>This is killing me!</i>

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:11.540
<i>I know how to ask!</i>

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:14.550
What?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.050
<i>I-Is she mad at me?!</i>

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:21.170
'Twas nothing. Mine eyes doth 
chanced to meet with thine!

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:23.060
I do beg your pardon

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:27.810
Well, if that's all... You were smiling 
about something, so I was curious

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.940
Oh, that's because I saw you 
working with a smile, Ko-chan

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.320
Huh? Was I smiling?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.590
Yeah. It was a super cute smile

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.070
Hifumin!

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.230
Y-Yes?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:45.080
I mean, not that it's 
a huge deal or anything...

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:49.080
But is it that unusual to see me smile?

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.220
No.

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.150
You've been smiling a lot lately.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:58.840
I know how steely-eyed 
you used to be while working,

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:00.900
so I'm reassured.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.290
It's not like I never smiled before!

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.720
Huh?!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:11.230
But as for earlier, the character models 
you guys submitted were looking good,

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:14.730
so I guess that's why I was smiling.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:19.270
Thank you...

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.030
You've learned to smile 
more yourself, Hifumin!

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.540
Finally relaxed that poker face of yours?

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:30.900
Oh yes, you have!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.040
Stop!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.420
<i>What in the world?!</i>

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:38.290
<i>No, don't be hasty. 
They're just having a conversation.</i>

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:44.430
<i>But the other day, Ko-chan complimented 
Hifumi-chan's meat and potatoes.</i>

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:51.670
<i>The shameful thing is, I can't just be glad she's learned to get along with others.</i>

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:56.460
Goodness, I don't often see 
you two talking amongst yourselves.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:57.660
What's up?

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.250
What? We need a reason to chat?

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.250
It's our little secret. Right, Hifumin?

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.740
Huh? Y-Yeah...

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:08.840
Oh, dear. You're going to make me jealous.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.500
Clearly, I'm interrupting.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:15.280
<i>Hifumi's sharp intuition 
for picking up on others' hints</i>

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:18.600
<i>was raising all sorts of red flags!</i>

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.570
I'll get out of your way, so please continue.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.890
Jeez, what's she even mad about?

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:30.040
<i>Come on, Ko-chan... Take a hint 
about how Rin-chan feels already!</i>

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.260
Oh, yeah.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.070
The meat and potatoes 
from the other day were really good.

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.490
Plan to make them again?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.680
Both the meat and potatoes were so tender,

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:43.160
<i>Hifumi knew the reason their relationship 
had never gotten anywhere all these years.</i>

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.210
and bursting with flavor...

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.240
<i>Ko's inability to take a hint!</i>

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:49.660
Why don't you... ask Rin-chan... 
to make some?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.840
Well, yeah, Rin's meat and 
potatoes are good, too.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:53.610
Right, right!

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:57.800
But I just can't stop thinking 
about how delicious yours were.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:01.990
<i>How dense... can you be?</i>

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:09.550
Oh, um... I lost the paper... 
that I wrote the recipe on...

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.920
So I can't make it... anymore.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.250
Oh, really? That's too bad.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.130
They were so good, too.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:21.020
<i>I'd better give Rin-chan the 
meat and potatoes recipe...</i>

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.500
<i>And send...</i>

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.530
It really didn't bother me, you know

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:31.460
But this is nice to have. Thank you

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.970
Right, hope it helps!

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:37.670
The secret ingredient is lots of love!!

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.790
I'm sure. Oh, by the way...

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.300
What were you two talking about earlier?

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.300
<i>We weren't doing anything!</i>

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:50.380
We were just saying how we've both 
become more expressive lately

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:54.460
<i>That's the truth. I hope it works.</i>

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:59.970
You certainly have. 
I think you're both trying really hard.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:01.310
I believe in you!

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:05.220
<i>Conflict resolved... Thank goodness.</i>

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:12.370
<i>Interacting with others is so taxing...</i>

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.340
<i>But I made a really good effort today.</i>

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:18.620
<i>However, all that effort's left me drained.</i>

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.840
<i>Time for a nap.</i>

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.260
Takimoto-san.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.270
I-I-I'm so sorry for sleeping!

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:32.580
Er, well, there are still five minutes 
of lunch break left, so that's not an issue.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.850
In fact, I'm sorry for waking you.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.230
You dropped your phone.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.960
Thank you very much...

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:41.980
Have you been sleeping enough?

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.980
Sleep is very important.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:49.930
Sleep deprivation can negatively affect 
your work, and more importantly, your health.

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:53.160
Sleeping in your chair may 
temporarily relieve your fatigue,

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:56.040
<i>I just want to be alone!</i>

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.370
but it's bad for your lower back.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:08.220
A girl had wandered into 
a mysterious wonderland.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.090
Beary, bear.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:11.470
A land which, curiously, 
was inhabited by plushies!

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:12.050
Beary, bear.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.550
<i>"I have to survive..."</i>

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.060
<i>She sneaks up from behind, and...</i>

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:16.690
<i>Gotcha!</i>

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.560
Bear, bear!

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.560
<i>Snip, snip!</i>

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.720
Turning the plushie into a kigurumi!

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.770
Thus disguised, the girl is able 
to blend in with the plushies.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.310
Clear your way of enemies 
as you hide among them

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.740
and uncover the secrets of this world!

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:38.780
I could keep doing this all day!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.540
Need I remind you that today's 
the deadline for the prototype?

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:46.250
I know! But...

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:50.190
If this doesn't go through, 
we'll have to cancel development, right?

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:55.010
Well, that's what happens 
when you lose all funding.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:58.870
Was it really okay for me to 
be the character designer?

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:02.710
I mean, you're more famous and 
more talented than me, Yagami-san.

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:07.490
What, so we wasted our time like idiots 
on something you have no faith in?

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:08.270
Huh?

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:15.490
I'm half kidding. I understand how you 
feel, but be more confident in yourself.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:16.740
Yun-san...

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:20.330
I agree... It'll go fine...

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.140
Hifumi-senpai...

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:29.170
On that note, let's have our last 
pre-prototype character team meeting.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.410
Right.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:35.540
Why didn't I join the character team?

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:38.520
Please don't feel that we're excluding you!

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:42.460
Yeah, I know. Go ahead, don't mind me.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.540
Right...

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:47.520
So, here's my progress report.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:50.750
I'm almost done correcting 
and retouching the visuals,

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.530
which should be ready in time for submission.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:57.530
Most of the models' errors and warnings
 have been taken care of.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:02.290
I'm working on refining the models 
as much as currently possible.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.710
The character team seems to be on track.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.880
Hazuki-san...

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.920
Wait, what happened?!

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:15.430
Oh, this? Call it a medal 
of valor, I suppose.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.100
It's a small price to pay if 
it means improving the game.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:21.420
By the way, Yagami.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.680
Y-Yes?

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.550
Once you're done, will you come to 
the meeting room with Takimoto-kun?

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.190
It's about that matter.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.220
Oh, sure.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.210
<b>A few minutes later</b>

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:39.200
Hello. Have you seen Hazuki-san?

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.290
She just went to the meeting 
room... You look tired.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:48.710
Yes. I was a fool to let her off with
 a mere forehead flick for spec changes.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.590
Oh... That explains it.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.340
Sorry to bug you when you're so busy.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.130
I wanted to ask you something, Takimoto-kun.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:59.090
I see...

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.770
I asked you once before,

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:06.600
but are you interested in replacing 
Yagami-kun as character team leader?

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.850
Um... Me...?

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:13.650
Thank goodness. At least this time 
you didn't completely shut down.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.610
What the heck happened last time?

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:20.620
Am I really... fit for the job?

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.100
You're more than qualified, based on skill.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:27.370
You're the one creating the main 
character models, aren't you, Takimoto-kun?

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:34.630
Plus, I'd like to remedy the current tendency
to rely on Yagami whenever there's an issue.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:37.270
This is for the future of the team.

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:44.050
Furthermore, I'm aware that you have 
a hard time communicating with others,

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:47.050
and also that you're 
getting better day by day.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:52.900
I...

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:57.400
I don't have big dreams like Aoba-chan...

00:18:57.730 --> 00:19:00.910
And I'm not as responsible as Yun-chan...

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:06.910
But they're both very kind, 
so I'm sure they'll follow my lead.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:11.650
I'm just afraid such a spineless 
leader would... well...

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:17.100
let everyone... down.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:22.680
I'm often second-guessing myself, too.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.560
You were even there to see it, Hifumin.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.680
When I stepped down as AD before.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.690
When I let everyone down...

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:37.070
So I'm happy just knowing 
the current team has faith in me.

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:40.580
I'd like to put the same faith in the team.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:46.120
Nothing that can happen will 
make me think less of you, Hifumin.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.580
I want you to believe in me.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:57.270
Er, sorry. I shouldn't be pushing 
you if you don't want to do this.

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:58.090
It's okay...

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:01.870
I know how hard you've worked, Ko-chan...

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.100
I've been by your side this whole time...

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.740
So... Okay.

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:13.230
I'll believe in your words, Ko-chan.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.900
Glad to hear that. Thanks.

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:24.030
It would seem my presence was unnecessary.

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:27.410
All right. Then to honor Takimoto-kun's 
resolve, among other things,

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.360
let's focus on getting 
this prototype approved.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.790
If you give it a try and things get 
too hard, I'll take your place.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:40.800
Don't you worry. People change, 
given new circumstances.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:44.550
Circumstances? Perhaps you 
should worry about yours.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:49.290
Hey, Umiko-kun. What's the matter?

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:54.980
"What's the matter?" You know full well.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:58.980
All of the programmers are waiting 
for you. Now please, hurry up.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.990
Wait! No more forehead flicks, please!

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:07.020
Will I have to... talk to Umiko-san... 
at meetings, too?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.690
How many times does this make?

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:12.000
W-Well, yeah. But she's really 
nice to responsible people.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:16.000
Wh-Wh-What should I do?!

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.260
You'll be fine.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:21.750
<b>Some days later</b>

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:21.750
Hello, I'm Yamato.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:25.760
I'd like to thank you for all of 
your hard work on the prototype.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.370
I see her around here sometimes.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:28.790
As this project is a completely new IP,

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:30.340
She's the producer from the publisher.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:32.030
I'm sure it was an endeavor to come up with

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:32.030
The whole team answers to her.

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:33.770
so many original ideas.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.850
Our company has reviewed the product, and...

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.610
...it was very well received.

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:45.500
Thank goodness!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:49.780
Let's keep up the good work and 
set our sights on the alpha version.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:52.790
That's a relief.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.220
We did it!

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:55.710
But of course!

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.910
Aoba-chan, Yun-chan...

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:02.840
As character team leader... 
I'll be counting on you...

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.030
Of course!

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:06.550
We're glad to have your leadership!

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:09.080
Right!
